# API Information


main: {
  kit: {
    info: {
      contact: {
        url: "https://github.com/r-spacex/SpaceX-API"
      }
      description: "Open Source REST API for launch, rocket, core, capsule, starlink, launchpad, and landing pad data."
      license: {
        name: "Apache 2.0"
        url: "https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0.html"
      }
      servers: [
        {
          description: "Production server (v5)"
          url: "https://api.spacexdata.com/v5"
        }
      ]
      title: "SpaceX REST API"
      version: "5.0.0"
      tagline: "Open-source REST API for SpaceX launches, rockets, capsules, cores, crew, payloads, pads, and Starlink data"
      homepage: "https://github.com/r-spacex/SpaceX-API"
      docs_url: "https://github.com/r-spacex/SpaceX-API/tree/master/docs"
      license_short: "Apache-2.0 — community project, not affiliated with SpaceX"
      license_md: `- Source code and data are released under the [Apache License 2.0](https://github.com/r-spacex/SpaceX-API/blob/master/LICENSE).
- Maintained by the [r-spacex](https://github.com/r-spacex) community; this project is **not affiliated with, endorsed by, or associated with Space Exploration Technologies Corp** (SpaceX).
- Attribution to the r-spacex project is appreciated when reusing data.
- Operational status and backups are published separately at [status.spacexdata.com](https://status.spacexdata.com) and [backups.spacexdata.com](https://backups.spacexdata.com).`
      about_md: `The [SpaceX REST API](https://github.com/r-spacex/SpaceX-API) is an open-source, community-maintained catalogue of SpaceX launches, vehicles, infrastructure, crew, and Starlink satellites. It is run by volunteer contributors at the [r-spacex](https://github.com/r-spacex) GitHub organisation and is independent of SpaceX itself. This SDK targets the \`v5\` base URL at \`https://api.spacexdata.com/v5\`.

What you can pull from the API:

- Past, upcoming, and "latest"/"next" launches with mission details and payloads.
- Rockets, cores, and capsules — including reuse history and current status.
- Launchpads and landing pads, with locations and status.
- Crew members, payloads, the Tesla Roadster trajectory, ships, and Starlink satellite TLE data.

The API is read-only and CORS-enabled, so it can be called directly from browser apps. No API key or authentication is required for the public endpoints. Published rate-limit numbers are not documented in the public docs; treat the service as best-effort and cache responses where possible.`
      entity_desc: {
        capsule: "Dragon capsule serial numbers with reuse counts, status, and mission history — `/capsules`."
        core: "First-stage booster cores, including reuse, landing attempts, and current status — `/cores`."
        crew: "Astronauts and crew members who have flown on SpaceX missions, with agency and status — `/crew`."
        landpad: "Landing pads and droneships used for booster recovery, with location and status — `/landpads`."
        launch: "Launch missions (past, upcoming, latest, next) with payloads, cores, links, and outcomes — `/launches`."
        launchpad: "Launch facilities such as LC-39A or SLC-40, with location, status, and associated rockets — `/launchpads`."
        payload: "Payloads carried on launches, including mass, orbit, customers, and manufacturer — `/payloads`."
        roadster: "Telemetry for the Tesla Roadster launched on Falcon Heavy's demo flight — `/roadster`."
        rocket: "Rocket families (Falcon 1, Falcon 9, Falcon Heavy, Starship) with specs and success rates — `/rockets`."
        ship: "Recovery and support ships in the SpaceX fleet, with roles, ports, and status — `/ships`."
        starlink: "Individual Starlink satellites with TLE orbital elements and launch references — `/starlink`."
      }
      auth: false
    }
  }
}
